@ 17.13.2 - Proto-Tocharian to Tocharian B
# citation: Nortaneous, from http://www.utexas.edu/cola/centers/lrc/eieol/tokol-TC-X.html and https://azargoshnasp.net/history/Tocharian/positionoftocharian.pdf Kʷ “usually but not always retained” “[E]penthesis [of /ə/] to break up ‘difficult’ consonant clusters (mostly in the coda?)”
	{ {a,ɛ}u, əw } > { au, u }
	{ {a,ɛ}i, əj } > { ai, i }
	{ ɔ, ɛ } > { o, e }
	w > ∅ / _j
	C:[+coronal]w > C:[+long]
	mn > nm / V_V
	s > ∅ / n_#
	∅ > t / :{ N_S, L_S }:
	ə > ∅ / _%, when unstressed